1. Mandatory item-level identity becomes physical-world infrastructure =E2=
=80=94 <strong>9.5/10 alpha</strong>

Thesis
<p>AGI cannot act safely on a physical world represented by ambiguous SKUs,=
 stale databases and unverifiable product histories. Until now, better phys=
ical identity was mostly an efficiency choice. The EU is turning it into a =
legal prerequisite.</p>
<p>On 20 July 2026 the European Commission made the <strong>Digital Product=
 Passport Registry operational</strong>. It stores unique product identifie=
rs and metadata, supports API registration, publishes machine-readable sema=
ntic models, and includes verification/logging. The first hard deadline is =
<strong>18 February 2027</strong>, when covered EV, LMT and industrial batt=
eries must have a battery passport. The Commission=E2=80=99s August guidanc=
e enumerates <strong>71 required battery-passport data points</strong>.</p>
<p>This is more than ESG/compliance plumbing. It is the beginnings of a sta=
ndardized <strong>physical-world state API</strong>:</p>
<p><code>physical object -&gt; persistent ID -&gt; verified attributes -&gt=
; lifecycle state -&gt; machine-readable API -&gt; authorized action</code>=
</p>
<p>That is directly useful to autonomous procurement, repair, recycling, in=
surance, resale, logistics, maintenance and robotics.</p>

