3. Rare-failure telemetry becomes a negative-data asset class =E2=80=94 <st=
rong>8.9/10</strong>

Thesis
<p>As autonomous systems get better, ordinary-success data gets cheaper whi=
le <strong>real failures become rarer and more valuable</strong>. The train=
ing objective shifts from =E2=80=9Clearn normal operation=E2=80=9D to =E2=
=80=9Cfind the 1-in-100k event that still kills the system.=E2=80=9D</p>
<p>2026 autonomous-vehicle research shows adaptive stress testing and diffu=
sion-based failure sampling can discover collision modes that ordinary Mont=
e Carlo simulation misses. Manufacturing research reaches the same structur=
al problem: mature systems generate extremely imbalanced failure datasets.<=
/p>
<p>This creates a new data-moat hierarchy:</p>
<p><code>success telemetry &lt; synthetic failures &lt; expert-labelled rea=
l failures &lt; longitudinal failure + remediation histories</code></p>
<p>The most valuable industrial datasets may therefore belong to businesses=
 that have spent decades inspecting things that break.</p>

Obscure public exposure: MISTRAS Group (NYSE: MG)
<p>MISTRAS is a ~$0.6B market-cap asset-integrity/NDT company spanning aero=
space, power, infrastructure, industrial facilities and pipelines. Its prop=
rietary software centralizes inspection and integrity data for predictive a=
nalytics and benchmarking.</p>
<p>The current business is also showing the exact physical bottlenecks the =
thesis predicts: in Q2 management said <strong>Aerospace &amp; Defense dema=
nd was temporarily outpacing testing capacity</strong>, and data-center/pow=
er investment was increasing demand for QA, inspection, commissioning and a=
sset-integrity work. Q2 revenue grew 4.2%, operating income 53.6%, and adju=
sted EBITDA 7%.</p>
<p>At roughly <strong>16=E2=80=9318x forward earnings</strong>, MG is much =
cheaper than most explicit AI-data companies, although the stock has alread=
y roughly doubled over the last year and remains labor-intensive with debt.=
</p>
<p>The optionality is not that MISTRAS suddenly becomes an AI software comp=
